      "title": "Tank or Treat 2026",
      "description": "<p>\ud83c\udf83 <strong>Tank or Treat at the Museum of the American G.I.</strong> \ud83c\udf83</p>\n<p>Looking for family-friendly Halloween fun? Join us at the Museum of the American G.I. on <strong>Sunday, October 25th, from 1:00\u20133:00 PM</strong> for an afternoon packed with spook-tacular games, crafts, and activities!</p>\n<p>Kids can test their skills at <strong>pumpkin chuckin&#8217; </strong>and<strong> pumpkin bowling</strong>, decode hidden messages using a <strong>Halloween spy decoder</strong>, play a game of <strong>spooky cornhole</strong>, or brave the mystery of the <strong>eyeball surprise</strong>. Create your own Halloween keepsakes at the <strong>make-a-mask station</strong> and <strong>slimy Halloween table</strong>, then treat your sweet tooth with <strong>marshmallow ghosts</strong>.</p>\n<p>Of course, the fun doesn\u2019t stop there\u2014explore the museum, enjoy the festive atmosphere, and snap some photos of your costumed crew with real WWII tanks and vehicles as the backdrop.</p>\n<p>\ud83d\udc7b <strong>Special Treat:</strong> Kids 12 and under who come in costume get in free!</p>\n<p>Bring the whole family and celebrate Halloween with history, fun, and a few frightfully good surprises!</p>",
